## 9. Linting & Code Quality

- Use each service's linter/formatter when present
- No dead code, no commented-out blocks
- Functions short; avoid nesting > 2 levels (prefer early return)
- One responsibility per function/class; prefer pure functions in `domain`
- No silent failures; use explicit domain exceptions
  (`AmbiguousSettlementException`, `IdempotencyKeyReusedException`, etc.), never a
  swallowed exception
- No unused dependencies; justify new deps in `docs/PLAN_PAYHUB.md` or an ADR, and confirm
  they don't violate the FinLedger integration boundary or introduce a shadow ledger
- Same patterns across services — a new consumer, saga activity, or adapter follows the
  shape of an existing one in another service

### Self-check before finishing a task

- Layers respected? (`domain` still zero-framework, in this service?) If not → FIX
- Business logic outside `domain`/`application`, or leaking into a BFF/consumer? → FIX
- A direct FinLedger REST call outside `LedgerPort`? → FIX
- A rail timeout mapped to a terminal state instead of `RECONCILIATION_REQUIRED`? → FIX
- A dual-write instead of outbox, or a distributed transaction instead of a saga step? → FIX
- Over-engineered relative to the current roadmap phase (plan §17)? → SIMPLIFY
- Understandable in <30s? → SIMPLIFY
- Idempotency, inbox/outbox, and compensation paths tested? → ADD tests if missing
- Tests pass locally for the affected service(s)? If not → FIX before committing

