## 10. CI/CD & Docker (engineering rules)

### Test execution in CI

- All tests run in CI exactly as they run locally — same profiles, same Testcontainers
  images (Postgres, Kafka, Temporal, Redis), same JDK version. No CI-only test skips.
- Integration tests use Testcontainers with real infra matching `platform/compose/`. Never
  H2, never embedded substitutes.
- ArchUnit tests run as part of the standard test phase per service — not optional.

### Docker image rules (per service)

- Each service's Dockerfile lives at `services/<name>/Dockerfile`, multi-stage build
  (build stage with Maven/JDK, runtime stage with JRE only, non-root user).
- A service must start with zero mandatory environment variables against
  `platform/compose/docker-compose.yml` defaults. Production overrides via env/Secrets.
- Every configurable value (datasource, broker endpoint, Temporal target, FinLedger base
  URL) is documented in that service's README section.
- No secrets baked into any image — ever, not even for local convenience.
- Images are architecture-portable: `linux/amd64` + `linux/arm64` via `docker buildx`.

### Forbidden CI/CD patterns

- Skipping tests in any pipeline stage
- Hard-coding secrets or credentials in workflow YAML
- Publishing a Docker image from a branch other than `main`
- Weakening branch protection or required checks without an ADR
- Using `latest` as the only tag — every release image also carries a semver tag
- Pinning FinLedger by `latest` instead of a semver/digest in `finledger/` config
